From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: amdv: auto-clear the DV VSIF hold at core teardown

dolby_vision_vsif_hold (patch 0002) is released only by userspace at disc
-session end. While set it swallows *every* DOVI->non-DOVI VSIF teardown,
and enable_amdv(0) - the definitive "DV core off" path taken on stop /
return-to-GUI - does not clear it. So if userspace ever fails to drop the
flag (player crash, abnormal stop, or a non-DV title started inside a held
session without the release call), the SDR teardown stays swallowed and the
sink is left with BT.2020 + the Dolby VSIF signalled over SDR/GUI pixels,
with no watchdog to recover.

Add a self-healing clear: enable_amdv(0) calls amdv_clear_vsif_hold(), which
drops both the hold request and the active latch. A disc-session segment swap
keeps the core enabled and never calls enable_amdv(0), so the hold still
survives the gaps it was written for; only a genuine full teardown clears it.

Clearing the flags is not on its own enough, which is why this lives next to
last_dst_format rather than beside the module_param. While the hold is set the
DOVI branch of send_hdmi_pkt() returns early and deliberately leaves
last_dst_format at FORMAT_DOVI, so the next segment resumes packet-identical.
At a real teardown the core stops presenting, send_hdmi_pkt() is never called
again, and that pending DOVI->SDR transition is therefore never emitted: the
sink keeps the Dolby VSIF latched over SDR/GUI pixels indefinitely.

Measured on an AM9 Pro 2026-08-30 after a Fallout S1D1 disc session: EOTF
stays DV-Std with dolby_vision_enable=N, dolby_vision_mode=5 and the core off,
hdmi_hdr_status reads DolbyVision-Std, and it survives stopping playback, a
Kodi restart and an HDMI PHY power cycle. Only a reboot clears it. The panel
is black on everything, GUI included, for as long as it lasts.

So emit the teardown here whenever the core goes down with DOVI still the last
signalled format, and put last_dst_format back to SDR to match.

--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
@@ -6984,6 +6984,47 @@
 /* #define HDMI_SEND_ALL_PKT */
 static u32 last_dst_format = FORMAT_SDR;
 
+/* Self-healing release for the disc-session VSIF hold: called from
+ * enable_amdv(0) so a full DV-core teardown (return-to-GUI / stop) is never
+ * left with the hold latched when userspace failed to clear it (player crash
+ * or abnormal exit). A stuck hold otherwise swallows the DOVI->SDR teardown
+ * and leaves BT.2020 + the Dolby VSIF signalled over SDR/GUI pixels.
+ *
+ * Dropping the two flags is not sufficient. While held, the DOVI branch of
+ * send_hdmi_pkt() returns early and deliberately leaves last_dst_format at
+ * FORMAT_DOVI so the next segment resumes packet-identical. At a genuine
+ * teardown the core stops presenting, so send_hdmi_pkt() never runs again and
+ * the pending DOVI->SDR transition is never emitted - the sink keeps the
+ * Dolby VSIF latched for good (survives stop, a Kodi restart and an HDMI PHY
+ * power cycle; only a reboot clears it).
+ *
+ * Emit that teardown here instead, whenever we are going down with DOVI still
+ * the last signalled format. Guarded on last_dst_format rather than on
+ * vsif_hold_active because a DV segment that presented after the swallowed
+ * transition clears the active latch while leaving the sink signalled DOVI
+ * just the same.
+ */
+void amdv_clear_vsif_hold(void)
+{
+	const struct vinfo_s *vinfo;
+
+	if (dolby_vision_vsif_hold)
+		pr_dv_dbg("clear stale VSIF hold at DV teardown (holder missed release)\n");
+	dolby_vision_vsif_hold = false;
+	vsif_hold_active = false;
+
+	if (last_dst_format != FORMAT_DOVI)
+		return;
+
+	vinfo = get_current_vinfo();
+	if (vinfo && vinfo->vout_device &&
+	    vinfo->vout_device->fresh_tx_vsif_pkt) {
+		pr_dv_dbg("send pkt: DV teardown with VSIF latched, signal SDR\n");
+		vinfo->vout_device->fresh_tx_vsif_pkt(0, 0, NULL, true);
+	}
+	last_dst_format = FORMAT_SDR;
+}
+
 static bool send_hdmi_pkt
 	(enum signal_format_enum src_format,
 	 enum signal_format_enum dst_format,
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.h
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.h
@@ -799,6 +799,7 @@
 extern bool force_stb_mode;
 extern unsigned int debug_dolby;
 extern unsigned int dolby_vision_flags;
+extern void amdv_clear_vsif_hold(void);
 extern uint amdv_mask;
 extern bool dolby_vision_on;
 extern bool amdv_core1_on;
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
@@ -6457,6 +6457,7 @@
 	if (!enable) {
 		if (dolby_vision_flags & FLAG_TOGGLE_FRAME)
 			pr_dv_dbg("clear stale TOGGLE_FRAME at DV teardown (bypass path missed gated clear)\n");
 		dolby_vision_flags &= ~FLAG_TOGGLE_FRAME;
+		amdv_clear_vsif_hold();
 	}
 }
